{:edb/db-before-t 6135 :edb/db-after-t 6136 :edb/tx-data [[13194139539448 50 #inst "2026-10-24T01:55:47.830Z" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221095 1074 "Let $t$ be the number of train tickets and $m$ be the number of museum tickets bought for $\\$72$.\n\nWe see that the graph passes through the point $(9,0)$. This means that the cost of $9$ train tickets and $0$ museum tickets is $\\$72$, which gives\n$9 d = 72$,\n\nSolving this for $d$, we get\n$d = 8$.\n\nTherefore, one train ticket costs $\\$8.00$." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221095 1074 "Let $t$ be the number of train tickets and $m$ be the number of museum tickets bought for $\\[math]72$.\n\nWe see that the graph passes through the point $(9,0)$. This means that the cost of $9$ train tickets and $0$ museum tickets is $\\[/math]72$, which gives\n$9 d = 72$,\n\nSolving this for $d$, we get\n$d = 8$.\n\nTherefore, one train ticket costs $\\[math]8.00$." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221540 1071 "Kai wants to book time in a recording studio. The studio charges $$40$ per hour, and there is also a one-time setup fee of $$30$. Kai has a budget of at most $$270$ for the session. If he can only book the studio for a whole number of hours, what is the maximum number of hours Kai can book?Kai can book the studio for at most\n{{field-1}}\nhours." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221540 1071 "Kai wants to book time in a recording studio. The studio charges $\\$40$ per hour, and there is also a one-time setup fee of $\\$30$. Kai has a budget of at most $\\$270$ for the session. If he can only book the studio for a whole number of hours, what is the maximum number of hours Kai can book?Kai can book the studio for at most\n{{field-1}}\nhours." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221542 1071 "Talia is ordering supplies for a science project. There is a one-time shipping fee of $$16$, and each supply kit costs $$17$. Talia must spend *at least* $$135$ in tota