 is the greatest number of lunches that can be ordered?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221545 1071 "A gym offers a monthly membership for $$120$ that allows unlimited class attendance. Without a membership, each class costs $$6.75$. What is the minimum number of classes a person must attend in a month for the membership to cost less than paying for classes individually?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221545 1071 "A gym offers a monthly membership for $\\$120$ that allows unlimited class attendance. Without a membership, each class costs $\\$6.75$. What is the minimum number of classes a person must attend in a month for the membership to cost less than paying for classes individually?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221548 1071 "A school principal plans to buy identical tablets for each of the $65$ teachers. The total budget for the purchase is $$11, 000$, which includes an $8 \\mathrm{\\% }$ sales tax. Which of the following is closest to the highest possible pre-tax price per tablet that the principal can afford within the budget?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221548 1071 "A school principal plans to buy identical tablets for each of the $65$ teachers. The total budget for the purchase is $\\$11, 000$, which includes an $8 \\mathrm{\\% }$ sales tax. Which of the following is closest to the highest possible pre-tax price per tablet that the principal can afford within the budget?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221549 1071 "Talia earns money by tutoring during the summer. She earns $$12$ per hour for the first $8$ hours she tutors in a week. After that, she earns $$18$ per hour for each additional hour. Talia saves $80%$ of her weekly earnings. What is the minimum number of additional hours she must tutor this week to save at least $$288$?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221549 1071 "Talia earns money by tutoring during the summer. She earns $\\$12$ per hour for the first $8$