 $30$ passengers at a time. Each adult ticket costs $\\$50$, and each child ticket costs $\\$30$. If the total revenue from selling tickets to one group was $\\$1, 200$, how many children were on the bus?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221572 1071 "Two customers bought the same kind of cheese and crackers at a grocery store. The first customer paid $$15.80$ for $2$ blocks of cheese and $3$ boxes of crackers. The second customer paid $$21.90$ for $3$ blocks of cheese and $2$ boxes of crackers.\n\nWhat is the cost, in dollars, of one box of crackers?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221572 1071 "Two customers bought the same kind of cheese and crackers at a grocery store. The first customer paid $\\$15.80$ for $2$ blocks of cheese and $3$ boxes of crackers. The second customer paid $\\$21.90$ for $3$ blocks of cheese and $2$ boxes of crackers.\n\nWhat is the cost, in dollars, of one box of crackers?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221574 1071 "A grocery store sells cherries for $$4.00$ per pound and peaches for $$2.50$ per pound. A nearby farmers market sells cherries for $$5.00$ per pound and peaches for $$6.00$ per pound. A particular order of cherries and peaches would cost $$36.50$ at the grocery store or $$60.00$ at the farmers market.\n\nHow many pounds of peaches are in this order?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221574 1071 "A grocery store sells cherries for $\\$4.00$ per pound and peaches for $\\$2.50$ per pound. A nearby farmers market sells cherries for $\\$5.00$ per pound and peaches for $\\$6.00$ per pound. A particular order of cherries and peaches would cost $\\$36.50$ at the grocery store or $\\$60.00$ at the farmers market.\n\nHow many pounds of peaches are in this order?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221586 1071 "A baseball coach is buying $x$ bats and $y$ helmets for a team practice. The coach needs to purchase at least $18$ items in total, but wants to spend no more than $$2