unds of peaches did he buy?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221704 1071 "![](images/e6/e63df4e7aec8090d851ed5defad6ddfe6363172508f3209e94abcf2fde3ec0dc.png)\n\nThe graph shows the possible combinations of the number of pounds of apples and peaches that could be purchased for $\\$24$ at a certain fruit stand. If Samuel purchased peaches and $4$ pounds of apples for a total of $\\$24$, how many pounds of peaches did he buy?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221705 1071 "![](images/f6/f60c95a8e0bb48a093fafa3754351a715572fcea7c1dd4740c61ecc0ca8f4621.png)\n\nThe graph shows the possible combinations of the number of notebooks and pens that could be purchased for $$21$ at a school supply store. If Mia purchased pens and $6$ notebooks for a total of $$21$, how many pens did she buy?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221705 1071 "![](images/f6/f60c95a8e0bb48a093fafa3754351a715572fcea7c1dd4740c61ecc0ca8f4621.png)\n\nThe graph shows the possible combinations of the number of notebooks and pens that could be purchased for $\\$21$ at a school supply store. If Mia purchased pens and $6$ notebooks for a total of $\\$21$, how many pens did she buy?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186221714 1071 "![](images/91/914332f3d9029e4e93706b7ba26ad751e7e7e7d181658046b4526dadaeb7a767.png)\n\nThe graph above represents the possible number of boxes of cupcakes and boxes of brownies a customer can buy at a bakery to spend exactly $$48.00$ total on the two types of baked goods. The price of each cupcake box is the same, and the price of each brownie box is the same. What is the price of one brownie box?One brownie box costs $$$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186221714 1071 "![](images/91/914332f3d9029e4e93706b7ba26ad751e7e7e7d181658046b4526dadaeb7a767.png)\n\nThe graph above represents the possible number of boxes of cupcakes and boxes of brownies a customer can buy at a bakery to spend exactly $\\$48.00$ total on the 